  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "The Bound Notebook",
    "overview": "Morning Pages is a notebook first and an app second. Every screen sits on warm cream paper; navigation is the notebook's cloth binding, a linen spine with a dashed stitch running its length; dates are set large in a literary serif, the way you would head a fresh page. The interface is quiet so the ink can be loud: one terracotta mark shows where you are, sage confirms that something is safe, and everything else is ink on paper.\n\nDensity is low and margins are generous. The person using it is half awake at 6 a.m., so nothing competes for attention and nothing needs deciding. Controls are standard web controls (links, buttons, lists) wearing the notebook's palette and type, never a costume of stationery: there are no faux page curls, leather textures or skeuomorphic rings.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "Warm paper ground in both themes: cream by day, warm charcoal by night, never pure white or pure black.",
      "Navigation as binding: a linen spine with a dashed stitch, collapsing to a tab bar below 900 px.",
      "Fraunces for dates and screen titles only; Atkinson Hyperlegible Next for every control and line of UI text.",
      "One accent at a time: terracotta marks the current place, sage marks \"saved\".",
      "Flat and ruled: hairline ink rules separate things; no cards, and only floating tools cast a shadow."
    ],
    "rules": [
      {
        "name": "The One Mark Rule",
        "body": "At most one terracotta element marks \"you are here\" on a screen; terracotta is never decoration, a heading colour or a background field.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Tinted Neutral Rule",
        "body": "Secondary text and lines are tints of ink, never grey; on linen and paper they must still clear 4.5:1 (checked by `tests/unit/contrast.test.ts`).",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Lettered Date Rule",
        "body": "Fraunces sets dates and screen titles and nothing else; it never appears in a button, label or list.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Ruled Page Rule",
        "body": "Lists and data rows are separated by full-width hairline rules, like a ruled page; they are never boxed in cards.",
        "section": "elevation"
      }
    ],
    "dos": [
      "Do put every colour through the `light-dark()` tokens in `src/styles/tokens.css`, so Paper and Night stay paired.",
      "Do keep text pairs at ≥ 4.5:1 and UI marks at ≥ 3:1 in every theme, and add new pairs to the contrast test.",
      "Do keep motion under 200ms (`--dur-quick` 120ms, `--dur-base` 180ms) with `--ease-out`, and let `prefers-reduced-motion` zero it.",
      "Do keep touch targets at 44px or more and respect safe-area insets on every edge.",
      "Do theme the browser surfaces: selection (terracotta at 22 %), caret, focus ring and scrollbar all come from the palette."
    ],
    "donts": [
      "Don't use pure white, pure black or neutral grey anywhere; neutrals are tinted from paper and ink.",
      "Don't box content in cards or nest containers; use ruled rows and whitespace.",
      "Don't use terracotta for headings, large fills or decoration (The One Mark Rule).",
      "Don't set controls or labels in Fraunces.",
      "Don't add skeuomorphic stationery, such as page curls, leather or spiral rings; the world lends palette, type, density and the stitched spine only."
    ]
  }
